etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4191396\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: asiaone.com\nSLUG: australia-nestory-irankunda-connor-metcalfe-turkey-world-cup-2026\nTEXT: Australia spoiled Turkey\'s return to the World Cup stage with a 2-0 victory in their Group D opener. Connor Metcalfe scored the second goal, following Nestory Irankunda\'s opening score. The Australians\' rock-solid defense repelled waves of Turkish attacks, with 21-year-old playmaker Arda Guler\'s efforts being thwarted by goalkeeper Patrick Beach. Turkey dominated possession but were unable to find the equalizer, with Abdulkerim Bardakci\'s shot being saved by Beach. The result puts Australia second in the group, behind the United States\' 4-1 win over Paraguay on Friday.\n\nID: 4191238\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: channelnewsasia.com\nSLUG: australia-win-2-0-spoil-turkiyes-return-world-cup-stage-6182131\nTEXT: Australia spoiled Turkey\'s return to the World Cup stage with a 2-0 win. Beach made several crucial saves, including one that diverted the ball onto the post after Abdulkerim Bardakci\'s shot. Okon-Engstler set up the opening goal, and Irankunda scored in the first half. Australia took the lead just seconds after Turkey\'s best chance, and Beach continued to make saves in the second half. The win leaves Australia level on three points with Group D leaders the United States, who they will meet in Seattle on Friday.\n\nID: 4191360\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: fakti.bg\nSLUG: 1060902-australia-beat-turkey-in-vancouver\nTEXT: Australia edged Turkey 1-0 in their World Cup opener, with goalkeeper Dean Leotaux making several crucial saves. The match was played in Vancouver and saw Australia\'s defense hold strong, with Zeki Celik, Kerem Akturkoglu, and Hakan Calhanoglu testing the Australian goal. Despite Turkey\'s efforts, Australia took an important step towards the elimination phase with a hard-fought victory.\n\n\n',)
