etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4192173\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: scrippsnews.com\nSLUG: steven-spielbergs-disclosure-day-opens-no-1-while-obsession-sensation-continues\nTEXT: Steven Spielberg\'s "Disclosure Day" opens at No. 1, while the obsession sensation continues with "Obsession". The film, which stars Emily Blunt, Josh O\'Connor and Colman Domingo, cost $115 million to make. Reviews have been strong (80% fresh on Rotten Tomatoes), but audience response wasn\'t overwhelming, with the movie landing a "B" CinemaScore. The film\'s opening weekend was driven by an older audience demographic, with 41% of moviegoers aged 45 and up. "Obsession", a Focus Features release, has exceeded its opening weekend of $17.2 million for four consecutive weekends, collecting $19 million in ticket sales to bring its North American haul to $188.3 million and its worldwide total to $286.5 million.\n\nID: 4192249\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: emirates247.com\nSLUG: 2590\nTEXT: "Disclosure Day", starring Emily Blunt, Josh O\'Connor and Colman Domingo, topped the box office with a production budget of $115 million. The film performed consistently across North America, attracting a broad audience with 41% of viewers aged 45 and over. Despite positive reviews, its audience reception was moderate, earning a "B" CinemaScore. The film\'s strong performance is threatened by competition from indie horror film "Obsession", directed by Curry Barker, which added $19 million in ticket sales over the weekend.\n\nID: 4192385\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: apnews.com\nSLUG: disclosure-day-spielberg-box-office-2afc250609da00480bdaaab5fca1e573\nTEXT: "Disclosure Day", directed by Steven Spielberg, has opened with a solid start, earning $44 million at the domestic box office. The film, starring Emily Blunt, Josh O\'Connor, and Colman Domingo, has received strong reviews (80% fresh on Rotten Tomatoes), but audience response was not overwhelming, with a "B" CinemaScore. The movie\'s success will depend on strong legs in the coming weeks, with Spielberg citing a potential for a great run through the summer.\n\n\n',)
