etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4192736\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: thestar.com.my\nSLUG: soccer-japan-battle-back-to-draw-2-2-with-netherlands-in-texas-thriller\nTEXT: Japan battled back to draw 2-2 with the Netherlands in a thrilling match in Texas. Japan took control of possession early, limiting openings for both sides. Hiroki Ito\'s defensive work frustrated Malen in the 34th minute, and Suzuki kept out a header from Tijjani Reijnders. Ritsu Doan\'s cross led to Nakamura almost scoring late in the half, but he pulled his shot wide. Ayase Ueda hit the side netting moments later.\n\nThe Netherlands threatened in the second half and earned a deserved reward when Van Dijk scored six minutes after the resumption. Japan levelled seven minutes later, with Nakamura driving a deflected strike into the bottom corner from Takefusa Kubo\'s cutback. The Dutch reclaimed the lead through Summerville, but Japan equalised again with two minutes remaining when Ogawa powered his header towards goal and Kamada\'s head deflected the ball past Verbruggen.\n\nID: 4190766\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: channelnewsasia.com\nSLUG: netherlands-use-pressure-drive-bid-elusive-world-cup-triumph-6181831\nTEXT: The Netherlands are putting pressure on themselves to perform well in the World Cup, but coach Ronald Koeman emphasizes the need to focus on their opening match against Japan in Dallas. Despite having been to the World Cup final three times, the Dutch have lost each time and are now among the leading contenders. Koeman believes his team has a strong foundation, but acknowledges that they need to improve in certain areas. He advises taking each game at a time and prioritizing the match against Japan, which he considers a difficult test.\n\nID: 4192586\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: ibtimes.sg\nSLUG: netherlands-vs-japan-world-cup-preview-predictions-lineups-87934\nTEXT: The Netherlands and Japan are set to face off in the World Cup, with Van Hecke expected to start for the Dutch. The Netherlands\' midfield battle could be crucial, with Frenkie de Jong dictating possession and Ryan Gravenberch and Tijjani Reijnders providing energy. Japan, meanwhile, will be without key players Kaoru Mitoma and Wataru Endo due to injury concerns.\n\n\n',)
