etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4192087\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: gulftoday.ae\nSLUG: iran-says-no-point-in-us-talks-after-beirut-strike-casting-doubt-on-deal\nTEXT: Iran\'s Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi stated that the US talks have become pointless after a strike in Beirut cast doubt on the deal. The warring parties released conflicting information about the contents of the agreement, with Iran insisting on maintaining control over the Strait of Hormuz and the US rejecting this. The deal also includes the fate of Iran\'s nuclear programme, particularly its stockpile of highly enriched uranium. Araghchi said the only way to deal with Iran\'s enriched uranium is to dilute it inside Iran, contradicting Trump\'s previous statement that the US would remove and destroy the uranium.\n\nID: 4191990\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: businesstimes.com.sg\nSLUG: iran-signals-no-deal-will-be-signed-trumps-sunday-timeline\nTEXT: Iran\'s top negotiator, Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf, stated that there is "no point" in continuing talks with the US if it lacks the "will and ability" to fulfill its commitments and stop Israel from bombing Lebanon. Iran warned that Israeli attacks on Beirut would not go "unanswered". The US responded, saying Hizbollah had attacked "completely unprovoked" and firing at its territory would not be tolerated. The two sides have been negotiating via mediators such as Pakistan and Qatar since the truce kicked in, with a draft of the MOU including the US allowing the release of $25 billion of frozen assets.\n\nID: 4191844\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: thedailystar.net\nSLUG: iran-says-no-point-us-talks-after-beirut-strike-casting-doubt-deal-4198696\nTEXT: Iran says there\'s no point in US talks after the recent strike in Beirut, casting doubt on a deal. Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu had promised that any agreement would include the removal of enriched nuclear material, but the strike in Beirut\'s southern suburbs against Hezbollah targets has raised concerns. The military carried out strikes, hitting a Hezbollah infrastructure site and killing at least three people and wounding six others in the Ghobeiry neighbourhood.\n\n\n',)
