etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4192178\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: scrippsnews.com\nSLUG: uk-intercepts-russian-shadow-fleet-tanker-for-first-time\nTEXT: The UK military has intercepted an oil tanker linked to Russia\'s shadow fleet in the English Channel for the first time. The tanker, Smyrtos, was seized by commandos and the UK\'s National Crime Agency in a successful operation. The Smyrtos, flagged from Cameroon, was sanctioned by the UK last year for its involvement in shipping Russian oil. The tanker\'s destination was Port Said in Egypt, but it had recently visited the Russian port of Luga Bay. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky applauded the UK action, while a Kremlin envoy, Kirill Dmitriev, accused Prime Minister Keir Starmer of using the detention as a distraction from the UK\'s migrant crisis.\n\nID: 4191488\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: thenews.com.pk\nSLUG: 1405854-british-armed-forces-intercept-russian-shadow-fleet-vessel-in-high-stakes-channel-operation\nTEXT: The British Armed Forces intercepted a Russian Shadow Fleet vessel in high-stakes Channel operation. According to the Ministry of Defense, the vessel will be monitored off the south coast as investigations remain active. The enforcement action in Britain\'s territorial waters was in accordance with domestic and international law, supported by aircraft from the Maritime Air Group, including an RAF P-8 aircraft. Defense Secretary Dan Jarvis praised the skill, professionalism, and courage of armed forces personnel involved in the operation. The interception is seen as a blow to Putin\'s illegal war, with Russia relying on its shadow fleet to fund the conflict in Ukraine.\n\n\n',)
