etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4192453\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: apnews.com\nSLUG: tyra-banks-sues-netflix-antm-docuseries-7efd641bce6c40313ad25b4034cd5b1f\nTEXT: Tyra Banks sues Netflix over ANTM docuseries, claiming the platform edited her interviews to make it appear she was trying to evade a sexual assault topic. According to the lawsuit, Banks\' lawyers argue that she wasn\'t given an opportunity to review the docuseries until a day before its release, and that she wasn\'t contacted for fact-checking after her interviews. The lawsuit also claims that other judges from the show, including those who consulted on the docuseries, may have held a grudge against Banks. As a result of the docuseries\' release, public reaction has been "swift and harsh", with even Banks\' own ice cream shop in Sydney being subject to review bombing on Google.\n\nID: 4190835\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: smh.com.au\nSLUG: surgical-manipulation-tyra-banks-sues-netflix-over-next-top-model-documentary-20260614-p606ls-html\nTEXT: Tyra Banks has filed a defamation lawsuit against Netflix, alleging the streaming giant manipulated footage from her interviews to create a false narrative in their documentary series "Reality Check: America\'s Next Top Model". The lawsuit claims Netflix selectively edited and omitted parts of the interviews, including a claim that Banks knowingly allowed a contestant to be sexually assaulted on her show. The documentary featured former contestant Shandi Sullivan, who alleged she was sexually assaulted by a guest at Model House during filming in Italy.\n\n\n',)
