etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4190768\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: channelnewsasia.com\nSLUG: scotland-squeeze-past-haiti-1-0-bag-first-world-cup-win-in-36-years-6181916\nTEXT: Scotland secured their first World Cup win in 36 years, defeating Haiti 1-0 on Saturday. John McGinn\'s deflected first-half goal gave Scotland the lead in the 28th minute, after a shot took a double deflection to land in the back of the Haiti net. Scotland struggled with Haiti\'s pace, but lacked clinical finishing from the Caribbean team, making their first World Cup appearance since 1974. Scotland top Group C with their first win in the tournament, while Haiti face five-time world champions Brazil on June 19.\n\nID: 4191401\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: asiaone.com\nSLUG: scotland-haiti-world-cup-2026-results\nTEXT: Scotland secured their first World Cup win in 36 years with a 1-0 victory over Haiti on June 13, 2026. John McGinn scored the winning goal in the 28th minute after a close-range effort by Che Adams was saved by Haiti\'s Johny Placide. The win puts Scotland top of Group C, ahead of Brazil and Morocco, who drew 1-1 earlier on Saturday. The Scottish supporters made the most of their return to the global stage, giving a lung-busting rendition of The Bonnie Banks of Loch Lomond before kickoff.\n\nID: 4190828\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: thedailystar.net\nSLUG: mcginn-gives-scotland-win-over-haiti-world-cup-return-4198271\nTEXT: Scotland secured a crucial World Cup win over Haiti with a 1-0 victory. Midfielder John McGinn scored the decisive goal in the 28th minute, assisted by Ben Gannon-Doak\'s lay-off. McGinn had earlier come close to scoring in the 17th minute, but his shot crashed off the post. Haiti\'s Ruben Providence was a threat on the wing, while Frantzdy Pierrot\'s towering header in the 85th minute went just wide. The win marks Scotland\'s first World Cup game since 1974, when they lost all three matches.\n\nID: 4190786\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: indiatoday.in\nSLUG: scotland-beat-haiti-first-world-cup-win-since-1990-2926314-2026-06-14\nTEXT: Scotland secured their first World Cup win since 1990 by defeating Haiti 1-0 in the 2026 tournament. The breakthrough goal came in the 28th minute, scored by John McGinn after a rebound from Che Adams\' saved shot. This goal made McGinn Scotland\'s oldest scorer at the World Cup finals, and he nearly doubled the lead before halftime. Despite Haiti\'s pressure and a few close calls, Scotland held on to secure their first World Cup victory in 36 years.\n\n\n',)
