etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4192676\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: krcgtv.com\nSLUG: mayhem-mars-euphoria-as-new-york-city-celebrates-knicks-first-championship-in-53-years\nTEXT: The New York Knicks celebrated their first NBA championship in 53 years with a euphoric parade, but the festivities were marred by mayhem and violence. Gunshots rang out in Times Square as rowdy fans clashed with police, smashing vehicles and structures. The celebrations were sparked by the Knicks\' Game 5 win over the San Antonio Spurs, with fans cheering outside Madison Square Garden. However, the jubilation quickly turned chaotic as fans attempted to scale buildings and climb onto school buses, while also trying to hitch a ride on a moving fire truck. The NYPD struggled to maintain order, with police officers facing vandalism and destruction of property.\n\nID: 4191130\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: nypost.com\nSLUG: crazed-knicks-fans-smash-cop-car-as-nba-finals-ecstasy-immediately-turns-violent\nTEXT: Fans of the New York Knicks went wild after their team\'s 94-90 victory over the San Antonio Spurs in Game 5 of the NBA Finals, but their celebration quickly turned violent. In the hours following the game, Knicks fans smashed up a cop car outside Madison Square Garden, with two individuals jumping on top of the vehicle and shattering its front windshield. The destruction also extended to MTA buses and school buses, as fans took out their frustrations on the surrounding transportation.\n\nID: 4192417\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: channelnewsasia.com\nSLUG: dozens-arrested-in-new-york-violence-after-knicks-win-title-6182816\nTEXT: Dozens were arrested in New York after the Knicks\' first NBA championship win, with 63 people taken into custody overnight. The celebrations turned violent as unruly crowds flooded the streets, with one person shot and four stabbed. Police cars were vandalized, including those with shattered windshields, while school buses were set on fire. Ten police officers were injured, including one who was punched in the face and another hit with a glass bottle.\n\n\n',)
