etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4192028\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: thenews.com.pk\nSLUG: 1405911-ebola-outbreaks-keep-defying-control-in-congo-despite-sustained-efforts-here-s-why\nTEXT: A new Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo is defying control, with health workers struggling to contain the spread due to a lack of cooperation from local residents. The outbreak, which began a month ago, has already claimed lives in the Kpangba displacement camp, with workers from the provincial health ministry, WHO, and aid agencies being forced away by reluctant locals who deny that two women have died from Ebola. The standoff has left health authorities flying blind, with 22 displaced persons sites in the Nizi health zone having no preventive measures in place aside from a few educational messages. The situation is particularly challenging due to the involvement of a rare species of Ebola for which there is no vaccine, and the epicentre being in an area affected by conflict.\n\nID: 4192047\nCREATED: 2026-06-14\nDOMAIN: japantimes.co.jp\nSLUG: congo-health-workers-ebola-containment-struggles\nTEXT: Health workers in the Democratic Republic of Congo\'s Nizi region are struggling to contain Ebola outbreaks due to local resistance. After two women died in the Kpangba displacement camp, health workers were forced away by angry locals who denied the cause of death. The provincial health ministry, World Health Organization, and aid agencies were unable to trace contacts due to local denial.\n\n\n',)
